! Silicon on the whole 4x4x4 grid, for an effective mass and site angular momenta.
!
! QE's own two-atom cell with two changes, one for each quantity this input is for.
!
! `nosym = .true.` and the full grid, because <L> and <S> are **axial vectors**:
! summing them over a symmetry-reduced wedge and calling the result the cell's is
! wrong in exactly the way summing a polar vector over a wedge is, and the escape
! that works here is the whole unshifted grid rather than a symmetriser. The
! effective mass does not need it -- it is one non-self-consistent run at a single
! k-point -- but running both quantities off one converged density does.
!
! The band count is deliberately *not* set here. The effective mass wants a window
! past the four occupied bands and asks for one at the call, because carrying the
! extra bands through the self-consistent run itself costs the quenching identity
! seven orders of magnitude: <L> comes out at 2.6e-16 with the default band count
! and at 2.0e-9 with `nbnd = 10`, on the same cell and the same conv_thr.
!
! conv_thr is 1e-10 rather than what a total energy needs, because a second
! derivative divides the eigensolver's own scatter by the square of the stencil
! width, and there is no reference to hide behind: the mass is checked against
! Elk and against a band structure computed along a line.
 &control
    calculation = 'scf'
 /
 &system
    ibrav = 2, celldm(1) = 10.2, nat = 2, ntyp = 1,
    ecutwfc = 12.0, nosym = .true.
 /
 &electrons
    conv_thr = 1.0d-10
 /
ATOMIC_SPECIES
 Si 28.086 Si.pz-vbc.UPF
ATOMIC_POSITIONS crystal
 Si 0.00 0.00 0.00
 Si 0.25 0.25 0.25
K_POINTS (automatic)
 4 4 4 0 0 0
